  "live_records": {
    "q-39993": {
      "dom_id": "step-q39993",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $u?$\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We compute the dot product between $u$ and each of the listed vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (-7)+8\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =5-7+16-15 \\\\  & =-1.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {w}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {w}_{4} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot (-5)+8\\cdot (-1)+(-3)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =15-5-8-6 \\\\  & =-4.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot x & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {x}_{4} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-1)+8\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-5-1+8-12 \\\\  & =-10.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the correct option is 'None of the listed'.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
