    "q-39914": {
      "dom_id": "step-q39914",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $u?$\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We compute the dot product between $u$ and each of the listed vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2+3-4-3 \\\\  & =-2.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {w}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {w}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 5+(-1)\\cdot 0+4\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =5-8+3 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot x & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {x}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 3+3\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =1+2+12-15 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the correct option is $w$ and $x$ only.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-39914-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$v$  only",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"42\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D42F TEX-B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">v</mi></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>  only"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
