    "q-74077": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74077",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$, which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $u?$\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We compute the dot product between $u$ and each of the listed vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =0-4-6+10 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {w}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {w}_{4} \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0-2+0+2 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot x & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {x}_{4} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =0-1-9-4 \\\\  & =-14.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the correct option is $v$ and $w$ only.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
