    "q-140122": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140122",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Given the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$, which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $u?$\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We compute the dot product between $u$ and each of the listed vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-5)+6\\cdot 7+7\\cdot 1+8\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-25+42+7-24 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {w}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {w}_{4} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 5+6\\cdot 7+7\\cdot (-7)+8\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =25+42-49-24 \\\\  & =-6.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot x & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {x}_{4} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 5+6\\cdot (-7)+7\\cdot 7+8\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =25-42+49-32 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the correct option is $v$ and $x$ only.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
