    "q-74079": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74079",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$, which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $u?$\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We compute the dot product between $u$ and each of the listed vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot 0+4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =5+6+0+8 \\\\  & =19.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {w}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {w}_{4} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-5-4+1+8 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot x & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {x}_{4} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =0+2-2-8 \\\\  & =-8.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the correct option is $w$ only.",
