    "q-39988": {
      "dom_id": "step-q39988",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -k\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ k \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that  $u⊥v.$ Find the value of $k.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that their dot product is equal to zero.\nFirst, let's calculate the dot product in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =k\\cdot k+(-5)\\cdot k+(-1)\\cdot 3+(-k)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-5k-3+3k \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-2k-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the dot product to zero, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2}-2k-3 & =0 \\\\ (k-3)(k+1) & =0 \\\\ k & =-1,3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-39988-a",
