    "q-140260": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140260",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 3 \\\\ 10b \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],v=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 10 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that $u⊥v$ and $u⊥w.$ What is the value of $a-4b?$",
      "worked_solution": "Given that $u⊥v$ and $u⊥w$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v=0 \\\\ u\\cdot w=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's consider the first equation $u\\cdot v=0.$ Calculating the dot product in terms of $a$ and $b$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot (-6)+3\\cdot 8+10b\\cdot 6+4\\cdot (-3) & =0 \\\\ -6a+24+60b-12 & =0 \\\\ -6a+60b & =-12 \\\\ -a+10b & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, for the second equation $u\\cdot w=0$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot (-10)+3\\cdot 6+10b\\cdot 10+4\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ -10a+18+100b+4b & =0 \\\\ -10a+104b & =-18 \\\\ -5a+52b & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the values of $a$ and $b$, we need to solve the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}-a+10b=-2 \\\\ -5a+52b=-9\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $-5$ and adding the result to the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2b=1\\,⟹\\,b=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $b=\\frac{1}{2}$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-a+10b & =-2 \\\\ -a+10\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} & =-2 \\\\ -a+5 & =-2 \\\\ a-5 & =2 \\\\ a & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that\n\n$$\na-4b=7-4(\\frac{1}{2})=5.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
