    "q-140259": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140259",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ b-1\\end{aligned}],v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ a \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}],$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ a+1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that $u⊥v$ and $u⊥w.$ What is the value of $a+2b?$",
      "worked_solution": "Given that $u⊥v$ and $u⊥w$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v=0 \\\\ u\\cdot w=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's consider the first equation $u\\cdot v=0.$ Calculating the dot product in terms of $a$ and $b$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ 2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-5)+(-2)\\cdot a+(b-1)\\cdot (-9) & =0 \\\\ 4-5-2a-9b+9 & =0 \\\\ -2a-9b & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, for the second equation $u\\cdot w=0$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & =0 \\\\ 2\\cdot b+1\\cdot (a+1)+(-2)\\cdot 3+(b-1)\\cdot (-1) & =0 \\\\ 2b+a+1-6-b+1 & =0 \\\\ b+a & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the values of $a$ and $b$, we need to solve the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}-2a-9b=-8 \\\\ a+b=4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second equation by $2$ and adding the result to the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7b=0\\,⟹\\,b=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $b=0$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =4 \\\\ a+0 & =4 \\\\ a & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that\n\n$$\na+2b=4+0=4.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
